    description: "**Mechanism.** limits.partial_results_reason == '' while analysis_incomplete == False. Spec §960 states 'Present only when analysis_incomplete: true', yet the key is emitted (empty string) on a complete analysis. A consumer using key-presence as the incompleteness signal (per §960) gets a false positive — the key is always there.\n\n**Consequence.** The documented CONDITIONAL-PRESENCE contract is violated by unconditional emission; consumers cannot use presence/absence of the field as a completeness signal.\n\n**Related (distinct).** Family of INV-virik / INV-lifik (constant/reserved-field sentinels) but partial_results_reason is a distinct limits-block field named in neither. Related to WI-zafid (completeness-signaling contract fires inconsistently; partial_results_reason set while flag false) — cross-link; that row is the broader completeness-signal channel, this is the specific §960 conditional-presence violation. Source: dogfood_tranche_07 F123.A3, deterministic frozen read."  # 442e
